{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788226806,"nonce":"sktdDMmaPdQ7Ynes30ZfHSaX2p8=","message":"THIRD ECHO INACCURACY ON THE SAME SURFACE, measured live 2026-08-31 (session 11, `65b03c2`). Adding it here rather than filing a fourth issue because it is the same defect shape: the trade surface reports a number that is not what the game holds.\n\n## `data.after` under-reports the bought stock by exactly the amount bought\n\nFinal `accept/3.5-dialog-verbs.py --phase 3` run: **101 PASS / 1 FAIL**, and the one failure is this.\n\nThe deal, with two distinct defs (the earlier same-def collapse is `be75bc4`):\n\n- BUY 10 x `ComponentIndustrial` (trader had 15)\n- SELL 5 x `MealSurvivalPack` (colony had 86)\n\n**The trade itself was CORRECT and is proven so.** `3.9g` passed: colony silver went 1600 → 1240, a delta of −360, exactly what `totals.colony_silver_post_deal − totals.colony_silver` promised pre-confirm. `3.6h` passed at `lines_with_action == 3`. `3.9b` `actually_traded`, `3.9c` session closed, `3.9k` zero red errors.\n\n**But `data.after` reported the colony holding 50 `ComponentIndustrial`, and an independent `things {def:\"ComponentIndustrial\"}` read taken straight afterwards reports 60** — `totals.count: 60`, 3 stacks. The goods arrived. The echo did not notice.\n\nSo the colony paid 360 silver, received its components, and the verb's own post-trade read says it still has the pre-trade count. An agent checking 'did my purchase arrive?' off `data.after` is told no.\n\n## The likely cause, to be confirmed by whoever takes it\n\n`3.9f`'s label says the post-trade counts are 'read BACK from the rebuilt deal'. A rebuilt `TradeDeal` enumerates what the colony can TRADE, not what it HAS — and the independent read shows **30 of those 60 are forbidden** (one stack of 30 at [134,127], `forbidden: true`). `RimWorld/TradeDeal`'s tradeable enumeration goes through the trader's willing-to-buy set and reachability, so forbidden and unreachable stock is invisible to it. If that is the mechanism, `after` is not a colony inventory at all and is mislabelled as one.\n\n**Which would make it the same trap as the clamp above:** a number that is correct for what it actually measures, presented as an answer to a different question.\n\n## Extra acceptance for this issue\n\n- `data.after` either reports true colony holdings, or is renamed and documented to say it reports tradeable stock — and if the latter, the trade verbs publish a true holdings figure alongside it, because 'did what I bought arrive' is the question an agent actually has.\n- A live check buys a def of which the colony already holds a FORBIDDEN stack, and asserts the post-trade figure against an independent `things` read. That fixture is what exposed this; without a forbidden stack present the two numbers agree and the bug hides.","files":null}]}